---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'How to Track Wishes – Methods for Every HoYo Game';
const description =
  'How to track wishes in Genshin, Star Rail and ZZZ: manual logging, history-file imports, and how to combine both — plus what each method can and cannot tell you.';
const updated = SITE.lastVerified;
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' }, { name: 'How to Track Wishes' }]}
  schema={[{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'How to track wishes in HoYo games',
    datePublished: '2026-10-08',
    dateModified: updated,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.brand },
  }]}
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>How to track wishes</h1>
    <div class="h1-bar"></div>
    <p class="lede">
      Every tracking method is a trade between effort, privacy and history depth. Here's the honest map —
      including where the browser-only <a href="/wish-tracker/">wish tracker</a> fits.
    </p>
    <div class="microline"><span>By {SITE.brand}</span><span>Updated {updated}</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Quick answer</h2>
    <p>
      For most players: import the past once (via the game's public wish-history page and a tool you trust),
      then log the future manually in a private tracker. You get full history plus a live pity counter that
      never touches a server.
    </p>

    <h2>The three methods</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>History depth</th><th>Privacy</th><th>Effort</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><a href="/wish-tracker/">Manual tracker (browser-only)</a></td><td>Forward only</td><td>Max — data never leaves the device</td><td>One tap per session</td></tr>
          <tr><td>History-file import tools</td><td>~6 months (game's retention window)</td><td>Depends on the tool's server</td><td>One-time + after each patch</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Spreadsheet discipline</td><td>As far as you keep it</td><td>Total</td><td>High</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>What the in-game history can and cannot tell you</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Can:</strong> every pull with timestamps and rarity — enough to reconstruct pity and 50/50 records.</li>
      <li><strong>Cannot:</strong> anything older than the retention window (~6 months) [VERIFY per game], or a lifetime luck profile — that only accumulates in your own log.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Setting up the hybrid workflow</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Import your history with a reputable tool to backfill the last six months.</li>
      <li>Enter your <em>current</em> pity and 50/50 state into the <a href="/wish-tracker/">tracker</a> as a baseline entry.</li>
      <li>Log pulls per session going forward — ten-pulls with the 5★ marked.</li>
      <li>Check <a href="/fifty-fifty-stats/">50/50 stats</a> monthly; watch trends, not single losses.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Base>
